  "description": "Seed registry for DimDegree. 'name' is the canonical value for DimDegree.name, a field of study rather than a titled program: 'bachelor' vs 'master' is not encoded here because DimDegree.name is UNIQUE and a posting almost never pins the level anyway. 'field' loads into DimDegree.field, the broad bucket that lets a posting asking for 'any engineering degree' match a specific one. 'level' has a column but no seed value: it describes an instance of education (what someone actually earned), so it belongs on UserEducation, not on the canonical program. 'aliases' are surface forms mapped to the name; there is no DegreeAlias table in schema.sql, so they widen prompt matching and are dropped at load time. A degree is what the posting asks the candidate to hold, so 'analista de sistemas' (a role) and 'ingeniero de datos' (a role) are never aliases here.",
